---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/sections/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/sections/Footer.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy - Macro" description="What happens to your data in Macro, in plain English.">
  <Nav />
  <main class="px-3 pt-22 sm:px-4 sm:pt-4">
    <div class="rounded-card bg-surface px-6 pt-16 pb-16 text-center sm:pt-44 sm:pb-20">
      <p class="eyebrow text-ios-blue">Privacy Policy</p>
      <h1 class="display mx-auto mt-5 max-w-3xl text-[clamp(2.6rem,6vw,4.5rem)]">Your data stays yours.</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-muted">Last updated: September 2026</p>
    </div>

    <article
      class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-3 pt-16 pb-8 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/75 [&_h2]:mt-12 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_h2]:font-display [&_h2]:text-2xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:tracking-[-0.03em] [&_h2]:text-ink [&_li]:mt-2 [&_p]:mt-4 [&_strong]:text-ink [&_ul]:mt-4 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6"
    >
      <p>
        Macro is a simple calorie and protein tracker made by an independent developer ({site.studioName}). This
        policy explains, plainly, what happens to your data.
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Macro doesn't have a server, doesn't run analytics, doesn't show ads, and doesn't ask you to create an
        account. Everything you log stays on your device and, if you turn on iCloud sync, in your own private iCloud
        account — never on our servers, because we don't have any.
      </p>

      <h2>What Macro stores</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The meals you log: calories, protein, and (if you turn tracking on) carbs, fat, and fibre, along with the
          label (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner, Snack) and time you logged them.
        </li>
        <li>Your daily goals and app preferences (e.g. which macros you track, when your day starts).</li>
        <li>
          If you turn on meal reminders, the app schedules local notifications on your device from the times you've
          logged meals. Those notifications never leave the device.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>This is all the app is for — it isn't used for anything beyond showing it back to you.</p>

      <h2>Where it's stored</h2>
      <p>
        By default, this data lives only in local storage on your device. If you turn on
        <strong>"Sync with iCloud"</strong> in Settings, it's additionally stored in your own private iCloud database, using Apple's CloudKit — governed by
        Apple's own privacy practices and your iCloud account. We (the developer) cannot see, access, or receive this
        data at any point; it never passes through a server we operate, because Macro doesn't have one.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can turn iCloud sync off at any time in Settings → iCloud &amp; Data, and you can permanently delete all
        logged meals from within the app (Settings → iCloud &amp; Data → Delete all meals), which also removes them
        from iCloud.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        Macro does not use any third-party analytics, advertising, or tracking SDKs. No data is sold, shared, or
        transmitted to any third party. The only outside service involved is Apple's iCloud/CloudKit, which is
        optional and under your control.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        This site doesn't use cookies, analytics or tracking scripts, and its fonts are served from the site itself
        rather than a third party.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Macro is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect any information from anyone, of
        any age — it simply stores what you choose to log, on your own device and iCloud account.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy ever changes, the update date at the top of this page will change too. Since the app doesn't
        collect contact details, we can't notify you directly — check back here if you're curious.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy or the app can be sent to <a
          href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}
          class="text-ios-blue hover:underline">{site.contactEmail}</a
        >.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
